==================================================
3. TYPOGRAPHY
==================================================

Use a refined editorial typography system.

Recommended heading font:

"DM Serif Display"
or
"Playfair Display"

Recommended body font:

"Inter"
or
"Manrope"

Headings should feel architectural and elegant.

Body text should remain extremely readable and modern.

Use:

- Large elegant headings
- Short paragraphs
- Generous line height
- Clear hierarchy

Avoid oversized typography that consumes the entire screen.

Avoid condensed fonts.

Avoid ALL-CAPS paragraphs.

Small uppercase labels are acceptable.

==================================================
4. GENERAL DESIGN LANGUAGE
==================================================

Use:

- Large whitespace
- Thin borders
- Soft rounded corners
- Very subtle shadows
- Editorial layouts
- Large photography
- Asymmetrical but balanced sections
- Minimal icons
- Clean cards
- Thin maroon accent lines
- Sand background blocks

Avoid:

- Excessive gradients
- Glassmorphism
- Neon colours
- Heavy shadows
- Huge rounded cards
- Excessive animations
- Dark sections everywhere
- Overuse of maroon
- Generic stock-business illustrations
- Excessive icons

The website should feel expensive because of its spacing, typography and photography — not because of visual effects.

